          "statement": "Let $X=(x_1,\\ldots,x_N)$ be a finite ordered list of distinct sites in $\\mathbb R^d$. If $K$ is strictly positive definite, then $K_X$ is invertible and $K_Xa=y$ has a unique solution for every $y\\in\\mathbb R^N$. If $K$ is strictly conditionally positive definite of order $m$ and $X$ is $m$-unisolvent for $\\Pi_{m-1}(\\mathbb R^d)$, then the augmented matrix in [[def-rbf-kernels-sites-and-augmented-interpolation]] is invertible and its system has a unique solution for every right-hand side."
        },
