          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Narcowich, Ward, and Wendland, Sobolev bounds on functions with scattered zeros, Math. Comp. 74 (2005), §§2.1–2.2",
                "url": "https://www.researchgate.net/publication/220577178_Sobolev_bounds_on_functions_with_scattered_zeros_with_applications_to_radial_basis_function_surface_fitting"
              }
            ]
          },
          "statement": "Let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be an admitted domain of [[def-rbf-kernels-sites-and-augmented-interpolation]], let $X\\subset\\Omega$ be finite and nonempty, and put $h=h_X$. Fix an integer $m\\ge1$ and let $J=\\dim\\Pi_{m-1}(\\mathbb R^d)$. There are constants $R,B,h_0>0$, depending only on $d,m,r_0,\\theta$, such that if $0<h\\le h_0$, then for every $x\\in\\overline\\Omega$ there are distinct nodes $y_1,\\ldots,y_J\\in X$ and real weights $\\lambda_1,\\ldots,\\lambda_J$ with\n$$|y_j-x|\\le Rh,\\qquad \\sum_{j=1}^J|\\lambda_j|\\le B,\\qquad p(x)=\\sum_{j=1}^J\\lambda_jp(y_j)\\quad(p\\in\\Pi_{m-1}(\\mathbb R^d)).$$\nNo lower bound on site separation is assumed."
