  {
    "id": "thm-best-rank-k-frobenius-matrix-approximation",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Best rank-k matrix approximation in Frobenius norm",
    "statement": "Let $A\\in\\mathbb F^{m\\times n}$, where $m,n\\ge1$, have a singular value decomposition\n$$ A=\\sum_{j=1}^{q}\\sigma_j u_jv_j^*,\\qquad \\sigma_1\\ge\\cdots\\ge\\sigma_q>0, $$\nwhere $q=\\operatorname{rank}(A)$. For an integer $k\\ge0$, put\n$$ A_k=\\sum_{j=1}^{\\min(k,q)}\\sigma_j u_jv_j^*, \\qquad \\delta_k^2=\\sum_{j=k+1}^{q}\\sigma_j^2 $$\nwith an empty sum equal to zero. Then $\\operatorname{rank}(A_k)\\le k$, $\\|A-A_k\\|_F=\\delta_k$, and every matrix $B$ with $\\operatorname{rank}(B)\\le k$ satisfies $\\|A-B\\|_F\\ge\\delta_k$.",
    "deps": [
      "def-finite-tensor-arrays-and-frobenius-inner-product",
