  {
    "id": "thm-tensor-train-storage-and-inner-product-cost",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Tensor-train storage and inner-product costs",
    "statement": "If a TT representation has mode sizes $n_k$ and bond sizes $r_0=r_d=1,r_1,\\ldots,r_{d-1}$, its core storage is exactly\n$$ \\sum_{k=1}^d n_kr_{k-1}r_k $$\nfield entries. If $A$ and $B$ have TT cores of bond sizes $r_k$ and $s_k$, respectively, their Frobenius inner product can be computed with\n$$ O\\!\\left(\\sum_{k=1}^d n_kr_{k-1}s_{k-1}r_ks_k\\right) $$\nscalar arithmetic operations and $O(\\max_k r_ks_k)$ additional workspace entries.",
