rrow0$. Given a tolerance, first choose $R$ so both tails are uniformly small and then pass to the limit on $[-R,R]$; this proves that the Abel limit equals the ordinary two-sided improper integral. As $\\varepsilon\\downarrow0$, $|\\alpha|\\to\\lambda/2$ and $\\arg\\alpha\\to-\\sigma\\pi/2$, so step 3.1 gives $\\sqrt\\pi(\\lambda/2)^{-1/2}e^{i\\sigma\\pi/4}=\\sqrt{2\\pi/\\lambda}e^{i\\sigma\\pi/4}$. [given, F1, F17, F22, F23, F24, F27, F28, F29, F33, F36, F38, F40, F41, step 3.1, algebra] ∎",
