  {
    "id": "lem-linear-cardinal-interpolant-on-an-edge",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "The affine edge interpolant is the unique degree-at-most-one cardinal polynomial",
    "deps": [],
    "dependency_level": 0,
    "statement": "Let $F$ be a field, let $a,b\\in F$ with $a\\ne b$, and let $y_0,y_1\\in F$. The unique polynomial $P\\in F[X]$ of degree at most one with $P(a)=y_0$ and $P(b)=y_1$ is\n$$P(X)=y_0+(y_1-y_0)\\frac{X-a}{b-a}.$$",
    "source_path": "items/lem-linear-cardinal-interpolant-on-an-edge.md",
