    "dependency_level": 4,
    "statement": "On every nondegenerate triangle, a point lies in the triangle if and only if its unique barycentric coordinates are all nonnegative; these coordinates also give the unique affine interpolant matching the three vertex data. Interpolants on adjacent triangles with common vertex data agree on their shared face. On an edge, the interpolant is the degree-at-most-one cardinal polynomial interpolant. For every nonempty finite site set, the nearest-site query returns a minimizer, breaks ties by least identifier, and reports correctly whether the query is inside or outside the convex hull.",
