  {
    "id": "lem-hlr-balanced-cluster-tree-size-and-depth",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "Size and depth of a balanced cluster tree",
    "statement": "Let $I$ be a finite ordered set of size $n\\ge1$, and let $b$ be an integer with $1\\le b\\le n$. In the balanced cluster tree of [[def-hlr-cluster-trees-and-geometric-admissibility]], every cluster at depth $h$ has size at most $\\lceil n/2^h\\rceil$. The tree has depth at most $\\lceil\\log_2(n/b)\\rceil$, at most $2n/b$ leaves, and at most $4n/b-1$ nodes.",
