    "id": "thm-hlr-core-svd-recompression-is-best-rank-tolerance",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Core-SVD recompression is best at the declared Frobenius tolerance",
    "statement": "Let $M=\\sum_s U_sV_s^*$ be the finite matrix input to [[alg-hlr-core-svd-recompression-with-tolerance]], and let $k$ and $\\delta\\ge0$ be its rank cap and Frobenius tolerance. If the algorithm returns **success** with rank $q$, its returned matrix $\\widehat M$ has rank $q$ and satisfies $\\|M-\\widehat M\\|_F=(\\sum_{j>q}s_j(M)^2)^{1/2}\\le\\delta$. No lower-rank matrix meets the same tolerance. If the algorithm returns **tolerance-not-met**, no matrix of rank at most $k$ meets the tolerance.",
