    "title": "Blockwise Frobenius errors propagate by disjoint block sums",
    "statement": "For any finite matrix partition into disjoint blocks, if each local residual satisfies $\\|E_b\\|_F\\le\\delta_b$, then the assembled residual satisfies $\\|E\\|_F\\le(\\sum_b\\delta_b^2)^{1/2}$. In particular, let $A,B$ be conformable finite real or complex matrices, and let $\\widetilde A,\\widetilde B$ be approximations with $\\|A-\\widetilde A\\|_F\\le\\epsilon_A$ and $\\|B-\\widetilde B\\|_F\\le\\epsilon_B$. If a successful block addition or block product from [[alg-hlr-block-addition]] or [[alg-hlr-block-product]] returns $\\widehat S$ or $\\widehat C$, with disjoint output blocks $b$ and local Frobenius errors $e_b\\le\\delta_b$, put $\\delta=(\\sum_b\\delta_b^2)^{1/2}$. Then\n\n$$\\|A+B-\\widehat S\\|_F\\le\\epsilon_A+\\epsilon_B+\\delta,$$\n\nand\n\n$$\\|AB-\\widehat C\\|_F\\le\\epsilon_A\\|B\\|_F+\\|A\\|_F\\epsilon_B+\\epsilon_A\\epsilon_B+\\delta.$$",
