    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice, let $n\\ge1$, and let $\\alpha,\\beta>-1$. Let $\\mu_{\\alpha,\\beta}$ be the finite positive Borel measure with density $(1-t)^\\alpha(1+t)^\\beta$ on $(-1,1)$ from [[lem-gauss-jacobi-weight-finite-moment-measure]]. Its moments through degree $2n-1$ are finite and its support is all of $[-1,1]$, so it is Gaussian moment data of order $2n-1$ in [[def-gauss-moment-data]]. The **$n$-node Gauss–Jacobi rule** is the general Gaussian rule $Q_n$ for this measure as defined in [[def-gauss-quadrature-rule]]: its nodes are the roots of the monic degree-$n$ orthogonal polynomial, and each weight is the integral of the corresponding Lagrange cardinal polynomial. This definition makes no accuracy or computed-node claim; local well-definedness is supplied by [[lem-gauss-jacobi-rule-data-well-defined]]."
