int table is chosen, proceed to the next endpoint. No upward division is attempted at zero.\n\n4. With both endpoint tables, form $I_m=\\operatorname{hull}(I_m(T_+),I_m(T_-))$ for every requested order, using endpoint minima and maxima. By $F'_m(T)=-F_{m+1}(T)<0$ from [[thm-boys-integral-identities-series-and-incomplete-gamma]], this encloses the full range over $\\mathcal T$. Return `success` only after every output radius is at most $\\varepsilon_a$ and, when relative tolerance is requested, the interval excludes zero and satisfies the relative-radius test in [[def-certified-evaluation-result-contract]]. Otherwise return `inconclusive`. Exhausting the finite refinement list or shared work counter also returns `inconclusive`. At a positive endpoint, return `range` only if a certified lower bound for some requested exact Boys value exceeds the largest finite magnitude of the format; a merely overflowing enclosure endpoint gives `inconclusive`. No branch promises success for every valid box or finite cap."
