  {
    "id": "lem-euler-pressure-solver-bracket-and-termination",
    "kind": "lemma",
    "title": "The safeguarded Euler pressure solver preserves its root bracket and terminates",
    "deps": [
      "alg-safeguarded-euler-star-pressure-solver",
      "thm-euler-star-pressure-root-and-vacuum-criterion",
      "alg-finite-budget-newton-for-vector-residuals",
      "alg-newton-correction-for-vector-residuals"
    ],
    "dependency_level": 6,
    "statement": "For admissible non-vacuum input data, the algorithm in\n[[alg-safeguarded-euler-star-pressure-solver]] terminates after at most $N$\nouter iterations and returns either a singleton exact root, a bracket\ncontaining the unique $p_*$ from [[thm-euler-star-pressure-root-and-vacuum-criterion]],\nor an explicit budget-exhausted status with that root still bracketed. After\n$k$ completed non-exact iterations the bracket width is at most\n$(3/4)^kP$. Thus any budget satisfying $(3/4)^N P\\le\\tau$ returns a\npressure-bracket status. No floating-point or nonlinear convergence guarantee\nis asserted.",
