          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Stokes velocity and pressure spaces and weak forms",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $d\\in\\{2,3\\}$ and let $D\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a nonempty bounded connected Lipschitz open set, where Lipschitz means that $\\partial D$ has a finite rigidly moved graph-chart atlas. Here $H^1_0(D)$ is the $H^1$-closure of $C_c^\\infty(D)$ ([[def-wkp-zero-as-a-sobolev-closure]], [[def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm]]). Since $D$ has finite measure, Holder makes every $L^2$ class integrable, so the zero-mean condition is well-defined ([[thm-holder-inequality-for-integrals]]). Define\n$$V:=H^1_0(D;\\mathbb R^d),\\qquad Q:=L^2_0(D):=\\{q\\in L^2(D;\\mathbb R):\\int_Dq=0\\}.$$\nEquip $V$ with $\\|v\\|_V:=\\|\\nabla v\\|_{L^2(D)}$ and $Q$ with $\\|q\\|_Q:=\\|q\\|_{L^2(D)}$. The local Poincare inequality [[lem-na-homogeneous-dirichlet-poincare]] makes the first a norm equivalent to the usual $H^1$ norm. For $v\\in V$, define $\\varepsilon(v):=(\\nabla v+\\nabla v^T)/2$ and $b(v,q):=-\\int_Dq\\,\\operatorname{div}v$. For viscosity $\\nu>0$, set $a_\\nu(u,v):=2\\nu\\int_D\\varepsilon(u):\\varepsilon(v)$, where $X:Y=\\sum_{i,j}X_{ij}Y_{ij}$. The continuous domain class is all bounded connected Lipschitz $D$; the exact mini-element mesh class is the narrower polygonal/polyhedral conforming affine simplicial class.",
