          "id": "thm-na-babuska-brezzi-kernel-coercivity",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "Babuska-Brezzi solvability by kernel coercivity and inf-sup",
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $V,Q$ be real Hilbert spaces, and let $a:V\\times V\\to\\mathbb R$ and $b:V\\times Q\\to\\mathbb R$ be bounded bilinear forms. If $Q=\\{0\\}$, the theorem reduces to Lax–Milgram on $V$ with $Z=V$ and $p=0$. Otherwise, if $Q\\ne\\{0\\}$, assume $V\\ne\\{0\\}$. Define $B:V\\to Q$ by $(Bv,q)_Q=b(v,q)$ and set $\\beta:=\\inf_{q\\ne0}\\sup_{v\\ne0}b(v,q)/(\\|v\\|_V\\|q\\|_Q)>0$. Suppose $Z:=\\ker B$ is closed and $a(z,z)\\ge\\alpha\\|z\\|_V^2$ on $Z$, with $\\alpha>0$. For every $F\\in V'$ and $G\\in Q'$, there is a unique $(u,p)\\in V\\times Q$ satisfying\n$$a(u,v)+b(v,p)=F(v),\\qquad b(u,q)=G(q),$$\nfor all $v\\in V,q\\in Q$. If $M_a=\\|a\\|$, then one stability bound is\n$$\\|u\\|_V\\le\\beta^{-1}\\|G\\|+\\alpha^{-1}(\\|F\\|+M_a\\beta^{-1}\\|G\\|),\\qquad \\|p\\|_Q\\le\\beta^{-1}(\\|F\\|+M_a\\|u\\|_V).$$",
