          "statement": "Input a dimension $d\\ge2$, a finite matching affine simplicial mesh $\\mathcal T_h$ whose boundary faces are paired by translations to form a periodic mesh, a constant velocity $\\beta\\in\\mathbb R^d$, one cell mean $U_K\\in\\mathbb R$ per cell, and a step $\\Delta t>0$. The output is either `CFL-inadmissible` or an updated vector of cell means $U^+=(U_K^+)_{K\\in\\mathcal T_h}$. Let $V_K=\\int_K1\\,dx$ be the cell volume and $A_F=\\int_F1\\,dS$ the face area. For each face $F\\subset\\partial K$, let $n_{K,F}$ be the outward unit normal, $b_{K,F}=\\beta\\cdot n_{K,F}$, and $K_F$ the neighboring cell across that periodic face. With $b^+=\\max(b,0)$ and $b^- =\\min(b,0)$, the upwind flux out of $K$ is\n$$\\widehat f_{K,F}=b_{K,F}^+U_K+b_{K,F}^-U_{K_F}.$$\n\nCompute\n$$\\lambda_K=\\frac{\\Delta t}{V_K}\\sum_{F\\subset\\partial K}A_Fb_{K,F}^+.$$\nIf $\\lambda_K>1$ for any cell, return `CFL-inadmissible` without updating the state. Otherwise, the **degree-zero upwind forward-Euler update** is admissible and its output is\n$$U_K^+=U_K-\\frac{\\Delta t}{V_K}\\sum_{F\\subset\\partial K}A_F\\widehat f_{K,F}.$$\nThis is the degree-zero specialization of [[def-pe04-upwind-dg-transport-discretization]].",
