    "statement": "Let $K$ be a cell in the one-dimensional interval or $d\\ge2$ matching affine-simplex branch of [[def-pe04-upwind-dg-transport-discretization]], and fix an integer degree $p\\ge0$. Let $(K,\\mathcal A,\\mu)$ be a finite measure space as in [[def-measure-space]], let $\\mathcal L^2(\\mu)$ have the raw measurable-function meaning of [[def-calligraphic-l-p-on-a-measure-space]], and let $W=\\mathbb P_p(K)\\subseteq\\mathcal L^2(\\mu)$. For $u\\in\\mathcal L^2(\\mu)$ define its **cellwise L2 projection relation** to be the set\n$$\\mathcal P_K(u)=\\left\\{p\\in\\mathbb P_p(K):\\int_K(u-p)w\\,d\\mu=0\\text{ for every }w\\in\\mathbb P_p(K)\\right\\}.$$\nFor a mesh, the broken relation is the product of these cell relations. The measure $\\mu$ is required to give positive measure to every nonempty relatively open subset of $K$ when existence and uniqueness are claimed. This definition does not itself assert that the set is a singleton. Whenever a later result proves that the relation has a unique member, write $\\Pi_Ku$ for that member.",
