    "id": "def-na-solenoidal-energy-weak-ns-velocity",
    "kind": "definition",
    "title": "Solenoidal energy weak velocity for incompressible Navier–Stokes",
    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice as inherited from [[def-na-evolutionary-incompressible-ns-weak-solution]]. Let $D$, $V$, $Q$, $V_\\sigma$, $H_\\sigma$, $a_\\nu$, and $c$ be as in [[def-na-evolutionary-incompressible-ns-weak-solution]]; the Stokes velocity and pressure spaces are $V=H^1_0(D)^d$ and $Q=L^2_0(D)$ as specified in [[def-na-stokes-zero-mean-pressure-and-velocity-spaces]]. For $f\\in L^2(0,T;L^2(D)^d)$ and $u_0\\in H_\\sigma$, a **solenoidal energy weak velocity** is a velocity $u\\in L^\\infty(0,T;H_\\sigma)\\cap L^2(0,T;V_\\sigma)$ that is weakly continuous into $H_\\sigma$, satisfies $\\operatorname{div}u=0$ almost everywhere, and obeys the scalar-test weak equation\n$$-\\int_0^T(u(t),v)_{L^2}\\eta'(t)\\,dt+\\int_0^T\\big(a_\\nu(u(t),v)+c(u(t);u(t),v)\\big)\\eta(t)\\,dt=\\int_0^T(f(t),v)_{L^2}\\eta(t)\\,dt+(u_0,v)_{L^2}\\eta(0)$$\nfor every fixed $v\\in V_\\sigma$ and $\\eta\\in C^1([0,T])$ vanishing near $T$. It also satisfies, for almost every $t\\in(0,T)$,\n$$\\frac12\\|u(t)\\|_{L^2}^2+\\nu\\int_0^t\\|\\nabla u(s)\\|_{L^2}^2\\,ds\\le\\frac12\\|u_0\\|_{L^2}^2+\\int_0^t(f(s),u(s))_{L^2}\\,ds.$$\nThis solenoidal definition does not itself assert a pressure exists in $L^{4/3}(0,T;L^2_0(D))$; that is a separate regularity conclusion.",
