    "title": "The mixed mini-element backward Euler Navier–Stokes scheme",
    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice as inherited from the energy-space conventions. Interpret each interval forcing average as a Bochner integral; its existence follows from the stated L2 forcing and the Bochner integrability criterion ([[def-countable-choice]], [[thm-bochner-integrability-criterion]]). Let $D$ be as in [[def-na-evolutionary-incompressible-ns-weak-solution]], let $\\mathcal T_h$ be a conforming shape-regular affine simplicial mesh of $D$, and let $V_h,Q_h,Z_h$ be the MINI spaces and weak divergence kernel of [[def-na-mini-element-p1-bubble-p1-spaces]] and [[def-na-discrete-weak-and-exact-divergence-free-spaces]]. For a partition $0=t_0<\\cdots<t_N=T$, write $\\tau_n=t_n-t_{n-1}$ and $f_h^n=\\tau_n^{-1}\\int_{t_{n-1}}^{t_n}f(t)\\,dt$. Given $u_h^0\\in Z_h$, a **backward Euler mini-element solution** is a sequence $(u_h^n,p_h^n)\\in V_h\\times Q_h$ satisfying, for $n=1,\\ldots,N$,\n$$\\left(\\frac{u_h^n-u_h^{n-1}}{\\tau_n},v_h\\right)_{L^2}+a_\\nu(u_h^n,v_h)+c(u_h^n;u_h^n,v_h)+b(v_h,p_h^n)=(f_h^n,v_h)_{L^2}\\quad(v_h\\in V_h),$$\n$$b(u_h^n,q_h)=0\\quad(q_h\\in Q_h).$$\nAll pressure variables use the zero-mean gauge $Q_h\\subset L^2_0(D)$. Restriction to $v_h\\in Z_h$ eliminates pressure. The equations are well-defined by [[lem-na-mini-be-scheme-is-well-defined]]; this definition claims no solver termination or error rate.",
