    "id": "thm-na-mini-be-smooth-velocity-error",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Smooth-branch velocity error for backward Euler MINI",
    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Assume the MINI mesh and time-partition hypotheses of [[def-na-mini-navier-stokes-backward-euler-scheme]]. Suppose $(u,p)$ is a strong solution of the no-slip Navier–Stokes equations with forcing $f\\in L^2(0,T;L^2(D)^d)$ and $u\\in W^{1,\\infty}(0,T;H^2(D)^d\\cap V_\\sigma)$ and $p\\in W^{1,\\infty}(0,T;H^1(D)\\cap L^2_0(D))$. Set\n$$M:=1+\\|u\\|_{W^{1,\\infty}H^2}+\\|p\\|_{W^{1,\\infty}H^1},\\quad M_u:=\\|u\\|_{L^\\infty V},$$\n$$M_\\infty:=\\bigl(\\|u_0\\|_2^2+C_P(D)^2\\nu^{-1}\\|f\\|_{L^2L^2}^2\\bigr)^{1/2},\\quad M_E:=\\nu^{-1/2}\\|u_0\\|_2+C_P(D)\\nu^{-1}\\|f\\|_{L^2L^2},$$\nand $\\Lambda:=1+C_D\\nu^{-3}M_u^4$, where $C_D$ depends only on the domain, dimension and the trilinear-form constant. For sufficiently fine time partitions satisfying $\\tau_{\\max}\\Lambda\\le\\tfrac12$, initialize by $u_h^0=P_{Z_h}u_0$ and choose any backward Euler MINI solution. Then\n$$\\max_{0\\le n\\le N}\\|u(t_n)-u_h^n\\|_2+\\nu^{1/2}\\left(\\sum_{n=1}^N\\tau_n\\|u(t_n)-u_h^n\\|_V^2\\right)^{1/2}\\le C_*\\bigl(hM+\\tau_{\\max}M^2\\bigr),$$\nwhere one may take\n$$C_*:=C_{D,\\mathrm{shape}}(1+\\nu)^2(1+\\nu^{-4})(1+T)^2(1+M_\\infty+M_E+M)^4\\exp(2T\\Lambda).$$\nHere $f$ is the forcing of the strong solution and $C_{D,\\mathrm{shape}}$ is independent of $h$, all time steps, and $\\nu$. The polynomial factor displays the positive and inverse viscosity powers produced by Young's inequalities and static Stokes projection. The explicit factor $\\nu^{-3}$ in $\\Lambda$ and exponential dependence on $T\\Lambda$ are retained; no Reynolds-uniform estimate is asserted. The separate instantaneous pressure assertion is addressed in Remarks.",
