          "statement": "Let $F=\\{(x_0,y,z):y_0\\le y\\le y_1,\\ z_0\\le z\\le z_1\\}$ be an oriented rectangle with normal $e_x$, and let $E$ be a $C^1$ vector field near $F$. Orient $\\partial F$ by the outward-normal-first convention. Then\n$$\\int_{\\partial F}E\\cdot t\\,ds=\\int_F(\\operatorname{curl}E)\\cdot e_x\\,dS=\\int_{y_0}^{y_1}\\int_{z_0}^{z_1}(\\partial_yE_z-\\partial_zE_y)(x_0,y,z)\\,dz\\,dy.$$\nThe identities for normals $e_y$ and $e_z$ follow by cyclic permutation of coordinates. Reversing a face orientation reverses both integrals."
