              {
                "title": "Olof B. Widlund, Introduction to the Design and Theory of Domain Decomposition Algorithms, DD20 Tutorial, §§87–88",
                "url": "https://cs.nyu.edu/~widlund/SD_rev_tutorial.pdf"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "def-pe26-feti-dp-dual-system-and-preconditioner",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "FETI-DP dual system and preconditioner",
          "deps": [
            "def-pe26-primal-interface-spaces-and-jumps",
            "def-pe26-discrete-harmonic-extension-and-schur-complement",
            "thm-pe26-primal-constraints-remove-floating-kernels",
            "def-pe26-scaled-averaging-and-bddc-preconditioner"
          ],
          "justified_by": [
            "prop-pe26-feti-dp-is-dual-schur-complement"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "statement": "Use $\\widetilde W$, $\\widehat W$, $E_0$, $R$, $B$ and $\\Lambda=\\operatorname{range}B$ as defined in [[def-pe26-primal-interface-spaces-and-jumps]] and [[def-pe26-scaled-averaging-and-bddc-preconditioner]]. Regard $\\bar E=R E_0$ as a projection on $\\widetilde W$. Since $\\ker B=\\operatorname{range}\\bar E=\\widehat W$, each class of traces with the same jump has a unique representative in $\\ker\\bar E$. Define $B_D^T:\\Lambda\\to\\widetilde W$ by assigning to $\\lambda\\in\\Lambda$ that unique representative $w$ with $Bw=\\lambda$ and $\\bar Ew=0$. This is the scaled right inverse; it obeys $BB_D^T=I_\\Lambda$ and $B_D^TB=I_{\\widetilde W}-\\bar E$. The latter identity makes the primal and dual projections complementary. In the two-subdomain edge case, its two entries are the coefficient-scaled jump weights complementary to those in $E_0$.\n\nThe **FETI-DP dual operator** and its preconditioner are\n\n$$F:=B\\widetilde S^{-1}B^T:\\Lambda\\to\\Lambda',\\qquad M_{\\rm FETI-DP}^{-1}:=B_D\\widetilde S B_D^T:\\Lambda'\\to\\Lambda.$$\n\nThe multiplier convention removes dependent row coordinates: $\\lambda$ is in $\\operatorname{range}B$, so no arbitrary multiplier component in $\\ker B^T$ is retained. Elimination of the partially assembled displacement and the resulting exact dual system are proved in [[prop-pe26-feti-dp-is-dual-schur-complement]].",
          "source_path": "items/def-pe26-feti-dp-dual-system-and-preconditioner.md",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Olof B. Widlund, Introduction to the Design and Theory of Domain Decomposition Algorithms, DD20 Tutorial, §§83–90",
                "url": "https://cs.nyu.edu/~widlund/SD_rev_tutorial.pdf"
              },
              {
                "title": "Jan Mandel and Bedřich Sousedík, BDDC and FETI-DP under Minimalist Assumptions, §§3.1 and 3.3",
                "url": "https://arxiv.org/pdf/0708.4031"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-pe26-log-edge-cutoff-and-discrete-sobolev",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Two-dimensional logarithmic edge cutoff estimates",
          "deps": [
            "def-pe26-scalar-substructuring-model",
            "lem-pe26-discrete-trace-schur-equivalence"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_level": 5,
          "statement": "Let $E$ be a side of a shape-regular polygon of diameter $H$ with a matching quasiuniform $P_1$ boundary mesh of size $h$. Let $\\theta_E$ be the piecewise-linear boundary function equal to $1$ at the interior nodes of $E$ and $0$ at the endpoints and all other boundary nodes. For\n\n$$\\|q\\|_{00,E}^2:=\\int_E\\int_E\\frac{|q(s)-q(t)|^2}{|s-t|^2}\\,ds\\,dt+\\int_E\\frac{|q(s)|^2}{\\operatorname{dist}(s,\\partial E)}\\,ds,$$\n\none has $\\|\\theta_E\\|_{00,E}^2\\le C(1+\\log(H/h))$. Also every continuous piecewise-affine $u_h$ on $\\Omega_i$ satisfies\n\n$$\\|u_h-\\overline u_{\\Omega_i}\\|_{L^\\infty(\\Omega_i)}^2\\le C(1+\\log(H_i/h_i))\\|\\nabla u_h\\|_{L^2(\\Omega_i)}^2.$$\n\nConsequently, for the edge mean $\\overline u_E$,\n\n$$\\|I_h(\\theta_E(u_h-\\overline u_E))\\|_{00,E}^2\\le C(1+\\log(H_i/h_i))^2\\|\\nabla u_h\\|_{L^2(\\Omega_i)}^2,$$\n\nwhere $I_h$ is nodal piecewise-linear interpolation on $E$.",
          "source_path": "items/lem-pe26-log-edge-cutoff-and-discrete-sobolev.md",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Olof B. Widlund, Introduction to the Design and Theory of Domain Decomposition Algorithms, DD20 Tutorial, pp. 25–33",
                "url": "https://cs.nyu.edu/~widlund/SD_rev_tutorial.pdf",
                "locator": "printed pp. 30–33, estimate (5) and its proof: the two-dimensional finite-element Sobolev inequality"
              },
              {
                "title": "Oliver Rheinbach, Parallel Scalable Iterative Substructuring, Chapter 2 §2.4, pp. 40–44",
                "url": "https://d-nb.info/983219192/34"
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "prop-pe26-feti-dp-is-dual-schur-complement",
          "kind": "proposition",
          "title": "FETI-DP is the exact dual Schur system",
          "deps": [
            "def-pe26-feti-dp-dual-system-and-preconditioner",
            "def-pe26-primal-interface-spaces-and-jumps",
            "thm-pe26-primal-constraints-remove-floating-kernels"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_level": 6,
          "statement": "Let $f\\in\\widehat W'$ and set $\\widetilde f=E_0^T f$. The constrained minimization problem\n\n$$\\min_{w\\in\\widetilde W,\\ Bw=0}\\left(\\tfrac12\\langle\\widetilde S w,w\\rangle-\\langle\\widetilde f,w\\rangle\\right)$$\n\nhas the saddle equations $\\widetilde S w+B^T\\lambda=\\widetilde f$, $Bw=0$. Eliminating $w$ gives the FETI-DP dual system\n\n$$B\\widetilde S^{-1}B^T\\lambda=B\\widetilde S^{-1}E_0^Tf.$$\n\nOn $\\Lambda=\\operatorname{range}B$ its matrix is positive definite, and the exact multiplier solution reconstructs the unique assembled interface solution $w\\in\\widehat W$.",
          "source_path": "items/prop-pe26-feti-dp-is-dual-schur-complement.md",
          "provenance": {
