          "statement": "Assume the model of [[def-pe26-scalar-substructuring-model]], all subdomain vertices primal, and the coefficient-scaled average of [[def-pe26-scaled-averaging-and-bddc-preconditioner]]. Let $P:=I-R E_0$ be the complementary jump projection on $\\widetilde W$, and let $\\|\\cdot\\|_{\\widetilde S}$ be the energy norm induced by the partially assembled Schur operator. Then\n\n$$\\|Pw\\|_{\\widetilde S}^2\\le C(1+\\log(H/h))^2\\|w\\|_{\\widetilde S}^2\\qquad(w\\in\\widetilde W),$$\n\nwhere $C$ depends only on the polygon/mesh shape bounds and bounded side count. It is independent of coefficient jumps, mesh size, subdomain diameter, and subdomain count.",
