          "dependency_level": 7,
          "statement": "For BDDC and FETI-DP built from the same positive definite partially assembled Schur operator, primal constraints, and scaled averaging, all eigenvalues of the two preconditioned operators other than $1$ agree with multiplicity. With the multiplier space fixed as $\\Lambda=\\operatorname{range}B$, neither operator has a zero eigenvalue; retaining all redundant row coordinates instead would add only multiplier null modes that are removed by this convention. The multiplicity of $1$ is not asserted to agree.",
