      ],
      "description": "{\"scope\": \"New Crouzeix-Raviart element/unisolvence/broken method/discrete Poincare/consistency/error; reuse reference-cell framework and continuous weak problem.\", \"proof_route\": \"Construct the face-average interpolant, bound jumps by local Neumann liftings and trace estimates, then prove consistency and use NA-30. Apply adjoint duality only with the declared smoothing exponent.\", \"examples\": \"one nonconforming face-average degree of freedom; broken-gradient norm; a solution below the trace regularity threshold.\"}",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "def-crouzeix-raviart-local-p1-element",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "The local P1 Crouzeix–Raviart element",
          "deps": [
            "def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes",
            "def-reference-finite-element-and-unisolvent-dofs"
          ],
          "statement": "Let $d\\ge2$ and let $K$ be a nondegenerate affine $d$-simplex with vertices\n$a_0,\\ldots,a_d$ and facets $F_i$ opposite $a_i$. Write\n$\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_d$ for its barycentric coordinate functions, so\n$\\lambda_i(a_j)=\\delta_{ij}$ and $\\sum_i\\lambda_i=1$. The local\nCrouzeix–Raviart polynomial space is $\\mathbb P_1(K)$, the real affine\nfunctions on $K$. Its face-average functionals are\n$$\\sigma_{K,F_i}(p):=\\frac1{|F_i|}\\int_{F_i}p\\,dS,\\qquad p\\in\\mathbb P_1(K).$$\nThe candidate dual shape polynomial associated with $F_i$ is\n$$\\phi_{K,F_i}:=1-d\\lambda_i.$$\nThe next item proves that these $d+1$ functionals are unisolvent and that the\ndisplayed polynomials form their dual basis. No pointwise continuity across\ndifferent cells is part of this local element.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Jean-Luc Guermond, MATH 661 Fall 2025, Part VIII, Chapter 36, Crouzeix–Raviart approximation",
                "url": "https://people.tamu.edu/~guermond/M661_FALL_2025/chap36.pdf",
                "locator": "§§36.2.1–36.2.2, PDF pp. 2–4: local affine polynomial space and face-average degrees of freedom."
              },
              {
                "title": "Joachim Schöberl, Numerical Methods for Partial Differential Equations, Chapter 25, Non-conforming Finite Element Methods",
                "url": "https://jschoeberl.github.io/iFEM/FEM/nonconforming.html",
                "locator": "§25.2, lines 276–290: the nonconforming P1 triangle and the midpoint/face degrees of freedom."
              }
            ]
          },
          "axiom_use": "No choice principle is used by this definition or finite-dimensional calculation.",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "level": 0,
          "strategy": "direct"
        },
        {
          "id": "def-crouzeix-raviart-fractional-sobolev-regularity",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Fractional Sobolev regularity on a simplex",
          "deps": [
            "def-fractional-slobodeckij-space-on-euclidean-space",
            "def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm",
            "def-countable-choice"
          ],
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $U\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a bounded open set,\n$0<r<1$, and let $q$ be a measurable real function on $U$. Define\n$$[q]_{H^r(U)}^2:=\\int_U\\int_U\\frac{|q(x)-q(y)|^2}{|x-y|^{d+2r}}\\,dx\\,dy,$$\nwith the diagonal integrand set to zero, and\n$H^r(U):=\\{q\\in L^2(U):[q]_{H^r(U)}<\\infty\\}$, using almost-everywhere\nclasses and norm $\\|q\\|_{H^r(U)}^2:=\\|q\\|_{L^2(U)}^2+[q]_{H^r(U)}^2$.\nFor $u\\in H^1(U)$, write $u\\in H^{1+r}(U)$ when each weak derivative\n$\\partial_j u$ belongs to $H^r(U)$, and define\n$$|u|_{H^{1+r}(U)}^2:=\\sum_{j=1}^d[\\partial_j u]_{H^r(U)}^2.$$\nFor vector fields, use the sum of the componentwise squared $H^r$ norms.\nUse these definitions on each cell $K$ and on the full domain $\\Omega$, with\n$\\|u\\|_{H^{1+r}(U)}^2:=\\|u\\|_{H^1(U)}^2+|u|_{H^{1+r}(U)}^2$. At $r=1$,\nset $H^1(U)=W^{1,2}(U)$, interpret $[q]_{H^1(U)}^2:=\\|\\nabla q\\|_{L^2(U)}^2$,\nand set $H^{1+r}(U)=W^{2,2}(U)$ with the ordinary integer-order norm and\nmembership of [[def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm]]. Thus\n$|u|_{H^2(U)}^2=\\sum_{j,k}\\|\\partial_k\\partial_j u\\|_{L^2(U)}^2$. The local\nseminorm is the restriction of the Slobodeckij convention in\n[[def-fractional-slobodeckij-space-on-euclidean-space]] to $U\\times U$.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "not-applicable"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Jean-Luc Guermond, MATH 661 Fall 2025, Part VIII, Chapter 36, Crouzeix–Raviart approximation",
                "url": "https://people.tamu.edu/~guermond/M661_FALL_2025/chap36.pdf",
                "locator": "Lemma 36.1, PDF p. 2, and Lemma 36.8, PDF pp. 6–7: W^{1+r,2} and face traces for r>1/2."
              },
              {
                "title": "Joachim Schöberl, Numerical Methods for Partial Differential Equations, Chapter 25, Non-conforming Finite Element Methods",
                "url": "https://jschoeberl.github.io/iFEM/FEM/nonconforming.html",
                "locator": "§25.2, lines 326–343: local H2 interpolation and reference-simplex scaling."
              }
            ]
          },
          "axiom_use": "Countable Choice is declared for the local Sobolev conventions; no Axiom of Choice is invoked.",
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "level": 0
        },
        {
          "id": "lem-crouzeix-raviart-continuous-poincare",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "A Poincare bound on a slab-bounded domain",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm",
