            "thm-tonelli-and-fubini-for-completed-product-measures",
            "thm-holder-inequality-for-integrals"
          ],
          "statement": "Let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be open and satisfy\n$a<x\\cdot e<b$ for a unit vector $e$ and all $x\\in\\Omega$, with $a<b$.\nThen every $v\\in H^1_0(\\Omega)$ satisfies\n$$\\|v\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}\\le(b-a)\\|\\nabla v\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}.$$\nThe argument assumes Countable Choice through the stated Sobolev,\nproduct-measure, and affine change-of-variables interfaces; it does not use the\nAxiom of Choice.",
          "provenance": {
            "statement": "literature-derived",
            "proof": "ai-altered"
          },
          "sources": {
            "references": [
              {
                "title": "Jean-Luc Guermond, MATH 661 Fall 2025, Chapter 3, Traces and Poincare inequalities",
