S}\\operatorname{osc}_K(U)^2.$$\nSince $b\\cdot\\nabla U$ is constant on $K$, this oscillation equals $h_K^2\\|f-\\Pi_K^0f\\|_2^2$.\n\nFor a separate definitional interface, consider the symmetric diffusion model $-\\operatorname{div}(A\\nabla u)=f$, where $A$ is a symmetric uniformly elliptic matrix field in the sense of [[def-uniformly-elliptic-divergence-form-operator]] and is Lipschitz on each cell. Its cell residual for a piecewise-affine $U$ is $R_K^A(U)=f+\\operatorname{div}(A\\nabla U)$, and its outward conormal-flux jump is the sum of $A\\nabla U\\cdot n_K$ from the two incident cells. Let $\\Pi_E^0$ be the $L^2(E)$ projection onto constants. The projected edge term $h_E\\|J_E^A-\\Pi_E^0J_E^A\\|_{L^2(E)}^2$ records nonconstant conormal flux. The reliability, contraction, and complexity results authored here concern $A=I$ only; this extension supplies notation and no coefficient-dependent theorem.",
