          "id": "def-supg-variational-multiscale-block-closure",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Finite-dimensional resolved–unresolved VMS split and residual closure",
          "deps": [],
          "statement": "Let $X_c$ and $X_f$ be finite-dimensional real vector spaces and set $X=X_c\\oplus X_f$; elements are written $(u_c,u_f)$, with $u_c$ the resolved component and $u_f$ the unresolved component. For a real vector space $Y$, let $Y^*$ be its space of real linear functionals. Let $A_{cc}:X_c\\to X_c^*$, $A_{cf}:X_f\\to X_c^*$, $A_{fc}:X_c\\to X_f^*$, and $A_{ff}:X_f\\to X_f^*$ be linear maps, with $A_{ff}$ invertible, and let $F_c\\in X_c^*$ and $F_f\\in X_f^*$. The linear equation on $X$ has block form\n$$\\begin{pmatrix}A_{cc}&A_{cf}\\\\A_{fc}&A_{ff}\\end{pmatrix}\\begin{pmatrix}u_c\\\\u_f\\end{pmatrix}=\\begin{pmatrix}F_c\\\\F_f\\end{pmatrix}.$$\nThe fine residual for a resolved vector $v_c$ is $r_f(v_c):=F_f-A_{fc}v_c$. Exact elimination gives $u_f=A_{ff}^{-1}r_f(u_c)$ and the Schur equation\n$$\\left(A_{cc}-A_{cf}A_{ff}^{-1}A_{fc}\\right)u_c=F_c-A_{cf}A_{ff}^{-1}F_f.$$\n\nA **residual closure** selects a linear map $T:X_f^*\\to X_f$ to approximate the exact inverse $A_{ff}^{-1}:X_f^*\\to X_f$. It defines $\\widetilde A_{cc}:=A_{cc}-A_{cf}TA_{fc}$, $\\widetilde F_c:=F_c-A_{cf}TF_f$, and the modeled fine component $\\widetilde u_f:=T r_f(\\widetilde u_c)$, where $\\widetilde u_c$ solves $\\widetilde A_{cc}\\widetilde u_c=\\widetilde F_c$. This is a finite-dimensional algebraic closure; an application to a PDE requires its own residual, spaces, invertibility, and approximation-defect analysis.",
