    "statement": "Let $d\\ge2$, let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a bounded connected polyhedral open set, and let a finite conforming nondegenerate simplicial mesh have connected cell adjacency. Let $V_h$ be continuous vector-valued P1 functions vanishing on the boundary, and let $Q_h$ be continuous scalar P1 functions with zero mean. Let $f\\in L^2(\\Omega;\\mathbb R^d)$, $\\nu>0$, $\\tau_K>0$, and $\\gamma\\ge0$. For the stationary Stokes specialization of [[def-supg-pspg-grad-div-stokes-forms]], define\n$$B_h((u_h,p_h),(v_h,q_h)):=\\nu(\\nabla u_h,\\nabla v_h)_\\Omega-(p_h,\\nabla\\cdot v_h)_\\Omega+(q_h,\\nabla\\cdot u_h)_\\Omega+\\gamma(\\nabla\\cdot u_h,\\nabla\\cdot v_h)_\\Omega+\\sum_K\\tau_K(\\nabla q_h,-\\nu\\Delta_Ku_h+\\nabla p_h)_K.$$\nFor the residual load, set $F_h(v_h,q_h):=(f,v_h)_\\Omega+\\sum_K\\tau_K(\\nabla q_h,f)_K$. Define\n$$\\|(v_h,q_h)\\|_{h}^2:=\\nu\\|\\nabla v_h\\|_2^2+\\gamma\\|\\nabla\\cdot v_h\\|_2^2+\\sum_K\\tau_K\\|\\nabla q_h\\|_{0,K}^2.$$\nThen this is a norm, $B_h(z_h,z_h)=\\|z_h\\|_h^2$, and the discrete problem $B_h(z_h,\\cdot)=F_h(\\cdot)$ has a unique solution satisfying $\\|z_h\\|_h\\le\\|F_h\\|_{h,*}$, where $\\|F_h\\|_{h,*}:=\\sup_{y_h\\ne0}|F_h(y_h)|/\\|y_h\\|_h$. The estimate controls pressure in the mesh-dependent gradient stabilization norm; it does not assert a mesh-uniform $L^2$ pressure bound or convergence.",
