          "dependency_level": 2,
          "statement": "Let $\\mathcal H_\\ell$ be the degree-$\\ell$ spaces on $\\mathbb S^2$ from [[def-three-dimensional-spherical-harmonic-space]], with surface measure of total mass $4\\pi$, and let $P_\\ell$ be orthogonal projection in $L^2(\\mathbb S^2)$. Define $\\Delta_{\\mathbb S^2}$ by the polar-coordinate identity $\\Delta=\\partial_{rr}+2r^{-1}\\partial_r+r^{-2}\\Delta_{\\mathbb S^2}$. Then $\\Delta_{\\mathbb S^2}g=-\\ell(\\ell+1)g$ for $g\\in\\mathcal H_\\ell$; for all smooth $v,w$ on the sphere, $\\langle v,\\Delta_{\\mathbb S^2}w\\rangle=\\langle\\Delta_{\\mathbb S^2}v,w\\rangle$; the spaces are mutually orthogonal and their algebraic sum is uniformly dense in $C(\\mathbb S^2;\\mathbb C)$. For smooth $f$, for every integer $m\\ge1$ there is a constant $C_m(f)$ such that $\\|P_\\ell f\\|_2\\le C_m(f)(1+\\ell)^{-m}$. For $g\\in\\mathcal H_\\ell$,\n$$\\|g\\|_\\infty\\le\\sqrt{\\frac{2\\ell+1}{4\\pi}}\\,\\|g\\|_2.$$\nFor each integer $p\\ge0$ there is $C_p$ independent of $\\ell,g$ such that $\\|g\\|_{C^p(\\mathbb S^2)}\\le C_p(1+\\ell)^{p+1/2}\\|g\\|_2$.\nThe angular Dirichlet form satisfies $-\\langle\\Delta_{\\mathbb S^2}g,g\\rangle=\\ell(\\ell+1)\\|g\\|_2^2$ for $g\\in\\mathcal H_\\ell$.\nFor every continuous $f$, the ordered partial sums $\\sum_{\\ell=0}^N P_\\ell f$ converge to $f$ in $L^2(\\mathbb S^2)$.",
