    "statement": "Let $\\Gamma$ be a polyhedral boundary as in [[def-bem-lipschitz-polyhedral-boundary-and-trace-spaces]]. A **conforming surface triangulation** $\\mathcal T_h$ is a finite collection of nondegenerate closed planar triangles covering $\\Gamma$, with disjoint relative interiors, such that two distinct triangles meet only in a common full edge, a common vertex, or not at all. For $T\\in\\mathcal T_h$, write $h_T=\\operatorname{diam}(T)$ and let $\\rho_T$ be the radius of the largest disk contained in $T$; the family is **shape regular** if $\\sup_{h,T}h_T/\\rho_T<\\infty$, and **quasi-uniform** if $\\inf_{h,T}h_T/h>0$ for $h=\\max_{T\\in\\mathcal T_h}h_T$.\n\nThe conforming **P0 density space** is $X_h=\\{\\lambda_h\\in L^2(\\Gamma):\\lambda_h|_T\\text{ is constant for every }T\\in\\mathcal T_h\\}$. The continuous inclusion $H^{1/2}(\\Gamma)\\hookrightarrow L^2(\\Gamma)$ follows because each chart Bessel norm controls its L2 norm and the fixed partition is finite. Hence every $\\lambda_h$ defines a bounded functional $v\\mapsto\\int_\\Gamma\\lambda_hv$ on $H^{1/2}(\\Gamma)$; thus $X_h\\subset H^{-1/2}(\\Gamma)$. This inclusion makes the single-layer Galerkin method conforming in its energy space.",
