    "title": "A planar rigid motion is controlled by its trace on a segment",
    "statement": "Let $\\Gamma_D$ be a fixed straight segment of length $L>0$ in the geometry of [[def-signorini-partial-trace-space]]. For every planar infinitesimal rigid motion $r(x)=a+\\omega Jx$, where $a\\in\\mathbb R^2$, $\\omega\\in\\mathbb R$, and $J=\\begin{pmatrix}0&-1\\\\1&0\\end{pmatrix}$, there is a constant $C=C(\\Omega,\\Gamma_D)$ such that\n$$\\|r\\|_{H^1(\\Omega)}\\le C\\|T_Dr\\|_{L^2(\\Gamma_D)}.$$",
