          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Assume the continuous trial-to-test operator is boundedly invertible with lower inf-sup constant $\\beta>0$, and let $\\Pi:V\\to V_r$ be the bounded Fortin map with $b(U_h,(I-\\Pi)V)=0$. For any exact solution $x=B^{-1}F$ and any $\\widetilde x_h\\in U_h$, define the practical residual estimator $\\eta=\\|F-B\\widetilde x_h\\|_{V_r'}$ and Fortin data oscillation $\\operatorname{osc}(F)=\\|F\\circ(I-\\Pi)\\|_{V'}$. Then\n$$\\beta^2\\|x-\\widetilde x_h\\|_U^2\\le\\eta^2+(\\|\\Pi\\|\\eta+\\operatorname{osc}(F))^2,\\quad \\eta\\le\\|b\\|\\|x-\\widetilde x_h\\|_U,$$\n$$\\operatorname{osc}(F)\\le\\|b\\|\\|I-\\Pi\\|\\inf_{z_h\\in U_h}\\|x-z_h\\|_U.$$\nFor the stated P1/R3 Poisson Fortin map, $\\operatorname{osc}(F_f)\\le C(\\sum_Kh_K^2\\|f-f_K\\|_{L^2(K)}^2)^{1/2}$, where $f_K=|K|^{-1}\\int_K f$; it vanishes for cellwise constant $f$.",
