    "statement": "Input an odd periodic grid with $N\\ge3$, a fixed $\\varepsilon>0$, particle count $P\\ge1$, total charge $Q$, total mass $M>0$, a state $Z=(z_1,\\ldots,z_P)$ with $z_p=(X_p,V_p)\\in\\mathbb R^{2d}$, and step $\\Delta t>0$. The grid, mass, and shape must satisfy the domains in [[def-periodic-pic-grid-and-inner-product]], [[def-periodic-pic-regularized-grid-interaction-kernel]], and [[def-periodic-pic-shape-assignment-and-gather]]; otherwise return status invalid-input. Use the exact-evaluation phase field of [[def-periodic-pic-regularized-grid-interaction-kernel]]:\n$$ F_p(Z)=\\frac1P\\sum_{r=1}^P\\mathbb K_{\\varepsilon,h}(z_p,z_r). $$ At each of four classical RK stages, evaluate this complete field at that stage's particle state: deposit every charge $Q/P$, subtract the neutralizing background, solve its zero-mean Poisson system with [[alg-periodic-pic-zero-mean-poisson-solver]], compute $E_h=-D^0\\phi_h$, and gather $E_h$ at each stage position $X_p$. Multiply the gathered field by $c=Q/M$ and return $F_p=(V_p,c(G_XE_h)_p)$, using that stage's velocity $V_p$. With $k_1=F(Z)$, $k_2=F(Z+\\frac{\\Delta t}{2}k_1)$, $k_3=F(Z+\\frac{\\Delta t}{2}k_2)$, and $k_4=F(Z+\\Delta t\\,k_3)$, return $$ Z^+=Z+\\frac{\\Delta t}{6}(k_1+2k_2+2k_3+k_4). $$\nEvery stage source is compatible by [[thm-periodic-pic-charge-conservation-and-neutralized-source]], and [[thm-periodic-pic-poisson-solver-returns-the-zero-mean-solution]] supplies each exact finite field solve. Thus no field-solve-failure branch occurs for admissible input. All operations use exact real or complex arithmetic; no floating-point stability or error bound is asserted."
