    "statement": "Fix $\\varepsilon>0$ and a finite signed Borel measure $\\mu$ on $\\mathbb T_L^d$ with total mass $Q$. Let $\\rho_\\varepsilon=\\eta_\\varepsilon*\\mu-Q/L^d$ and let $\\phi_\\varepsilon$ be its unique zero-mean periodic Poisson potential from [[thm-periodic-pic-continuum-regularized-poisson-kernel-is-smooth]]. Put $E_\\varepsilon=-\\nabla\\phi_\\varepsilon$. Use the shape and periodic centered-difference Poisson operator of [[def-periodic-pic-shape-assignment-and-gather]] and [[def-periodic-pic-grid-and-inner-product]]. Let $s_h=P_h^\\varepsilon\\mu-Q/L^d$, let $A_h\\phi_h=s_h$ with $\\bar\\phi_h=0$, set $E_{h,j}=-D^0\\phi_h$, and gather $G_hE_h$ using the same shape. Define\n$$ C_{\\rm dep}=\\frac{C_\\eta\\|\\eta_\\varepsilon\\|_\\infty}{Z_{\\min}}\\|\\mu\\|_{\\rm TV},\\quad C_{\\rm FD}=\\frac1{12}\\sum_{a=1}^d\\|\\partial_a^4\\phi_\\varepsilon\\|_\\infty,\\quad C_{\\rm src}=C_{\\rm dep}+C_{\\rm FD}, $$ where $C_\\eta,Z_{\\min}$ are from [[lem-periodic-pic-shape-partition-and-quadrature-bound]]. Put $$ C_3=\\frac16\\left(\\sum_{a=1}^d\\|\\partial_a^3\\phi_\\varepsilon\\|_\\infty^2\\right)^{1/2},\\qquad C_{\\rm int}=\\frac{C_{\\eta,E}+\\|E_\\varepsilon\\|_\\infty C_\\eta}{Z_{\\min}}, \\quad C_{\\eta,E}=\\frac{L^d}{12}\\sum_{a=1}^d \\sup_{x,y\\in\\mathbb T_L^d}\\left|\\partial_{y_a y_a}[\\eta_\\varepsilon(y-x)E_\\varepsilon(y)]\\right|_2 . $$ For vector fields, $\\|V\\|_\\infty=\\sup_x|V(x)|_2$ (the maximum of Euclidean lengths for grid fields); the derivatives in $C_{\\eta,E}$ use this same Euclidean norm. Then the source $s_h$ is compatible and $$ \\|G_hE_h-\\eta_\\varepsilon*E_\\varepsilon\\|_\\infty \\le L^{d/2}h^{2-d/2}\\left(\\gamma_{N,L}C_{\\rm src}+C_3\\right) +C_{\\rm int}h^2. $$\nThe displayed $\\gamma_{N,L}$ is the actual finite-grid inverse/derivative norm of [[thm-periodic-pic-poisson-residual-to-gathered-force-bound]] and satisfies $\\gamma_{N,L}\\le L/4$. Thus for $d\\in\\{1,2,3\\}$ this fixed-$\\varepsilon$ force error tends to zero 