    "statement": "Fix $\\varepsilon>0$, grid width $h$, particle count $P\\ge1$, and final time $T>0$. Apply classical RK4 from [[alg-periodic-pic-classical-rk4-step]] to the autonomous finite-dimensional PIC system\n$$ \\dot Z=F_{\\varepsilon,h}(Z),\\qquad (F_{\\varepsilon,h}(Z))_p=\\frac1P\\sum_{r=1}^P \\mathbb K_{\\varepsilon,h}(z_p,z_r),\\qquad z_p=(X_p,V_p). $$ Let $Z(t)$ be an exact solution on $[0,T]$. Assume $F_{\\varepsilon,h}$ is $C^4$ on an open set containing a common compact convex tube $\\mathcal T$; the exact path, all numerical states, and every RK4 stage generated from both the exact and numerical starting states lie in $\\mathcal T$; and all derivatives of $F_{\\varepsilon,h}$ through order four are bounded there. Choose a uniform step $0<h_t\\le h_0$ with $h_0>0$, initialize exactly, and retain every time $t_k=kh_t\\le T$ for integers $k\\ge0$; $T/h_t$ need not be an integer. The stage hypotheses concern each step ending by $T$. Put $$ L_F=2L_{\\varepsilon,h},\\qquad L_*=L_Fe^{L_Fh_0}, $$ and choose $C_4$ so that the exact-start defect on this tube is at most $C_4s^5$ for admitted steps $0<s\\le h_0$ ending by $T$. The local-order supplier gives such constants for a sufficiently small positive $h_0$ under the stated smoothness and tube assumptions. Then, for every grid time $t_k=kh_t\\le T$, $$ \\|Z_k-Z(t_k)\\|_2\\le \\begin{cases} C_4\\dfrac{e^{L_*T}-1}{L_*}h_t^4,&L_*>0,\\\\[4pt] C_4Th_t^4,&L_*=0. \\end{cases} $$\nThe tube, exact-solution, and stage-admissibility hypotheses are conditional; this is a fixed-$\\varepsilon$, fixed-grid finite-particle time error, not a continuum or singular-force estimate."
