          "id": "def-isoparametric-curved-cell-map",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Admissible isoparametric curved cells",
          "deps": [
            "def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "statement": "Fix a reference matching affine simplicial mesh as in [[def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes]]. An admissible curved cell is the image of a closed reference simplex $\\widehat K$ under a map $F_K\\in C^2(\\widehat K;\\mathbb R^d)$ that extends to a diffeomorphism on a neighborhood, is orientation preserving, and satisfies $0<j_0\\le J_K:=\\det DF_K\\le j_1$ and $\\|DF_K\\|+\\|(DF_K)^{-1}\\|+\\|D^2F_K\\|\\le C_F$. The physical cells have disjoint interiors, cover the domain up to their shared facets, and maps agree on each common reference facet under the prescribed affine facet identification. Define the volume metric $G_K=DF_K^TDF_K$, volume factor $J_K=\\sqrt{\\det G_K}$, and for a reference facet parametrization $\\widehat f$ the surface metric $G_{K,\\widehat f}=D(F_K\\circ\\widehat f)^TD(F_K\\circ\\widehat f)$ and surface factor $\\sqrt{\\det G_{K,\\widehat f}}$. The positive-Jacobian lower bound is the admissibility certificate; it is not inferred from a drawing or from Delaunay quality.",
          "source_path": "items/def-isoparametric-curved-cell-map.md",
