          "dependency_level": 1,
          "statement": "Let $\\widehat\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^d$ be a bounded reference domain and let $\\Phi,\\Phi_h:\\overline{\\widehat\\Omega}\\to\\mathbb R^d$ be cellwise $C^2$ admissible maps with matching traces, positive Jacobians, and common image topology. The exact and approximate domains are $\\Omega=\\Phi(\\widehat\\Omega)$ and $\\Omega_h=\\Phi_h(\\widehat\\Omega)$. Define $e_0=\\|\\Phi-\\Phi_h\\|_{L^\\infty(\\widehat\\Omega)}$ and $e_1=\\|D\\Phi-D\\Phi_h\\|_{L^\\infty(\\widehat\\Omega;op)}$. A geometry approximation claim must separately state bounds on $e_0,e_1$, both Jacobian lower bounds, and boundary-trace compatibility; none follows from the word “isoparametric.”",
