          "dependency_level": 1,
          "statement": "Assume AC and Countable Choice. In dimension two let $K=\\Psi(\\widetilde K)$, where $\\widetilde K$ is a shape-regular affine triangle of diameter comparable to $h_K$, and $\\Psi$ extends to a $C^2$ diffeomorphism on a neighborhood of $\\overline{\\widetilde K}$. Assume $\\|D\\Psi\\|_\\infty+\\|D\\Psi^{-1}\\|_\\infty+\\|D^2\\Psi\\|_\\infty+\\|J_\\Psi^{-1}\\|_\\infty$ are uniformly bounded. Let $v$ denote its continuous representative and set $I_Kv=(I_{\\widetilde K}(v\\circ\\Psi))\\circ\\Psi^{-1}$, the mapped nodal P1 interpolant. For $v\\in H^2(K)$, $\\|v-I_Kv\\|_{L^2(K)}\\le C h_K^2\\|v\\|_{H^2(K)}$ and $|v-I_Kv|_{H^1(K)}\\le C h_K\\|v\\|_{H^2(K)}$, with $C$ uniform over the family.",
