          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Under the finite partition hypotheses of [[def-intersection-volume-conservative-remapping]], let $P_0(\\mathcal T)$ be the target cellwise-constant subspace of $L^2(\\Omega)$. For every source piecewise-constant $v$, $Rv$ is the $L^2$ orthogonal projection of $v$ onto $P_0(\\mathcal T)$, hence $\\|Rv\\|_2\\le\\|v\\|_2$. It preserves total mass, $\\int_\\Omega Rv=\\int_\\Omega v$, and if all $v_i\\ge0$ then every target value $(Rv)_j\\ge0$.",
