          "dependency_level": 2,
          "statement": "Let $A=D\\Phi$ and $A_h=D\\Phi_h$ be orientation-preserving cell-map derivatives with $\\det A,\\det A_h\\ge j_*>0$, $\\|A\\|_{op},\\|A_h\\|_{op}\\le M$, and $\\|A-A_h\\|_{op}\\le e_1$. For every unit reference-facet normal $\\widehat n$, define the surface Jacobians $J_\\Gamma(A)=\\|\\operatorname{cof}(A)\\widehat n\\|$, $J_\\Gamma(A_h)=\\|\\operatorname{cof}(A_h)\\widehat n\\|$, and mapped unit normals $n_\\Gamma(A)=\\operatorname{cof}(A)\\widehat n/J_\\Gamma(A)$ and $n_\\Gamma(A_h)=\\operatorname{cof}(A_h)\\widehat n/J_\\Gamma(A_h)$. Then\n$$\\|\\operatorname{cof}(A)-\\operatorname{cof}(A_h)\\|_{op}+|J_\\Gamma(A)-J_\\Gamma(A_h)|+|n_\\Gamma(A)-n_\\Gamma(A_h)|\\le C(d,M,j_*)e_1.$$\nThe surface Jacobian agrees with the Gram-metric factor in [[def-isoparametric-curved-cell-map]].",
