          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\widehat\\Omega=[-1,1]^2$, let $\\mathcal T_h$ be a matching shape-regular affine triangulation, and put $\\Phi(x,y)=(x,y+x^2/4)$. Let $I_h$ be the vertexwise P1 interpolant and $\\Phi_h(x,y)=(x,y+I_h(x^2/4))$. In the notation of [[def-curved-domain-geometry-approximation]], there is a constant $C$ depending only on the shape-regularity bound such that $e_0\\le Ch^2$ and $e_1\\le Ch$. For sufficiently small $h$, $\\det D\\Phi_h\\ge1/2$, and $\\Phi_h$ is globally one-to-one on the square. The exact map has $\\det D\\Phi=1$ and a global inverse $(X,Y)\\mapsto(X,Y-X^2/4)$.",
