          "dependency_level": 2,
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\widehat\\Omega$ be bounded, let $\\Phi,\\Phi_h$ be the geometry maps of [[def-curved-domain-geometry-approximation]] and assume each is a global orientation-preserving $C^1$ diffeomorphism from $\\widehat\\Omega$ onto its image, with $J_h\\le J^*$ and $u$ is $L_u$-Lipschitz on the union of their images. On $\\Omega_h=\\Phi_h(\\widehat\\Omega)$ let $\\mathcal S=(S_i)_{i=1}^m$ and $\\mathcal T=(T_j)_{j=1}^n$ be finite families of Lebesgue-measurable sets of positive measure satisfying\n$$|\\Omega_h\\setminus\\textstyle\\bigcup_i S_i|=|\\Omega_h\\setminus\\textstyle\\bigcup_j T_j|=0,\\qquad |S_i\\cap S_{i'}|=0\\ (i\\ne i'),\\qquad |T_j\\cap T_{j'}|=0\\ (j\\ne j').$$\nThus each family is a finite measurable partition up to null sets as required by [[def-intersection-volume-conservative-remapping]]. Let $v_S$ be source-piecewise-constant data with finite $L^2$ error. Assume the exact target projection error below is finite. Define $P_Tq$ on each target cell by its exact cell average, $\\eta_S=\\|u-v_S\\|_{L^2(\\Omega_h)}$, and $\\eta_T=\\|u-P_Tu\\|_{L^2(\\Omega_h)}$. If $R$ is the exact overlap remap, then\\n$$\\|u\\circ\\Phi-(Rv_S)\\circ\\Phi_h\\|_{L^2(\\widehat\\Omega,J_h)}\\le L_u e_0\\sqrt{J^*|\\widehat\\Omega|}+\\eta_S+\\eta_T,$$\\nwhere $e_0=\\|\\Phi-\\Phi_h\\|_\\infty$ and $\\|z\\|_{L^2(\\widehat\\Omega,J_h)}^2=\\int_{\\widehat\\Omega}|z|^2J_h$.",
          "source_path": "items/thm-overlap-remap-error-from-approximation-and-geometry.md",
