          "statement": "For every tolerance $0<\\tau\\le\\sigma/4=1/4$, the algorithm [[alg-delaunay-seeded-curved-uniform-nvb-refinement]] with square boundary angle $\\alpha=\\pi/2$ and nonincident-feature separation $\\sigma=1$ terminates after finitely many three-generation cycles. Its reference triangles remain right isosceles with minimum angle $\\pi/4$, all interfaces match, and every curved cell map is orientation preserving. Pointwise on each cell, if $a_K$ is an affine parametrization of its reference triangle, then the induced metric $G_{\\Phi,K}=(D(\\Phi\\circ a_K))^TD(\\Phi\\circ a_K)$ has spectral condition number $\\kappa_2(G_{\\Phi,K})\\le(81/16)\\kappa_2(G_{\\mathrm{ref},K})$, where $G_{\\mathrm{ref},K}=(Da_K)^TDa_K$. The returned maximum curved-cell diameter is at most $\\tau$. This is a guarantee for this square/shear family; it asserts no general Delaunay minimum-angle theorem, adaptive complexity bound, or 3D shape bound.",
