    "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\widehat\\Omega=(-1,1)^2$ carry a finite matching affine triangular mesh $\\mathcal T$ as in [[def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes]]. Let $\\Phi,\\Phi_h:\\overline{\\widehat\\Omega}\\to\\mathbb R^2$ be continuous and $C^1$ on each closed triangle, with matching traces on shared edges, and suppose $\\|D\\Phi\\|_\\infty+\\|D\\Phi_h\\|_\\infty\\le M$, $e_0=\\|\\Phi-\\Phi_h\\|_\\infty$, and $e_1=\\|D\\Phi-D\\Phi_h\\|_{L^\\infty;op}$. Let $G$ be a scalar physical boundary lift on an open convex neighborhood containing both images and every segment joining corresponding image points, with $\\|DG\\|_\\infty\\le L_1$ and $\\|D^2G\\|_\\infty\\le L_2$. Define the piecewise pullback gradients by $\\nabla_{pw}(G\\circ\\Phi)=D\\Phi^T\\nabla G(\\Phi)$ and $\\nabla_{pw}(G\\circ\\Phi_h)=D\\Phi_h^T\\nabla G(\\Phi_h)$, and set\n$$\\ell_{\\partial,h}(w)=\\int_{\\widehat\\Omega}\\big(\\nabla_{pw}(G\\circ\\Phi)-\\nabla_{pw}(G\\circ\\Phi_h)\\big)\\cdot\\nabla w,\\qquad w\\in H^1_0(\\widehat\\Omega).$$\nWith the $H^1$ dual norm, $\\|\\ell_{\\partial,h}\\|_{(H^1_0)^*}\\le 2(L_1e_1+ML_2e_0)$. Thus the geometry-induced boundary-lift contribution to the Strang load defect is $O(e_0+e_1)$.",
