      "description": "{\"scope\": \"Define isoparametric cell maps, positive Jacobian/admissibility certificate, shape regularity with bounded map/inverse derivatives, surface metric and geometry approximation. Prove interpolation/scaling and Strang geometry-defect bounds on a stated curved-domain family. Define a concrete 2D mesh-generation/refinement procedure consuming robust predicates and Delaunay primitives; prove only stated angle/termination guarantees with boundary-angle and feature-size hypotheses. Define L2 projection and conservative intersection-volume remapping; prove cell mass conservation, positivity for nonnegative overlap weights, and error from a stated approximation/geometry bound. 3D slivers require independent quality conditions; 2D Delaunay angle facts do not remove them.\", \"proof_route\": \"Pull back gradients/forms, estimate Jacobian/cofactor/normal differences and boundary lifting residual. For refinement use packing/feature-size argument with explicit termination preconditions; preserve NA35's distinct refinement complexity contract. Transfer uses exact partition-of-unity intersection measures; numerical clipping consumes certified predicates and returns unresolved if degeneracy cannot be certified. Curved DG metric identities need a proved discrete geometric conservation identity before PE04 extension.\", \"examples\": \"curved disk, inverted map detection, 3D sliver, moving-grid mass transfer.\"}",
