          "dependency_level": 3,
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. On $[-1,1]^2$, the exact shear $\\Phi(x,y)=(x,y+x^2/4)$ maps each straight reference edge to a straight or parabolic arc. Its determinant is $1$. On any shape-regular affine mesh, the nodal P1 geometry map satisfies $e_0\\le Ch^2$, $e_1\\le Ch$, and $J_h\\ge1/2$ for small enough $h$. Consequently its Laplace tensor differs from the exact pulled-back tensor by at most $Ch$ in $L^\\infty$.",
