          "deps": [],
          "justified_by": [],
          "dependency_level": 0,
          "statement": "For an integer $d\\ge1$, put $w_d(t)=(1-t)^{d-1}$ on $[0,1]$ and, for $n\\ge0$, define\n$$\\phi_n(t):=\\frac{(-1)^n}{n!}(1-t)^{-(d-1)}\\frac{d^n}{dt^n}\\bigl(t^n(1-t)^{n+d-1}\\bigr).$$\nThe quotient extends to a polynomial of degree $n$. These polynomials are pairwise orthogonal in $L^2(w_d\\,dt)$, with\n$$\\phi_n(0)=(-1)^n,\\qquad \\operatorname{lc}(\\phi_n)=\\binom{2n+d-1}{n},\\qquad \\int_0^1w_d\\phi_n^2\\,dt=\\frac1{2n+d}.$$\nConsequently, for every $p\\ge0$ the squared norm of endpoint evaluation $q\\mapsto q(0)$ on $\\mathbb P_p([0,1])$ with this weighted $L^2$ norm is exactly $(p+1)(p+d)$.",
