        {
          "id": "lem-hp-weighted-analytic-corner-pointwise-control",
          "kind": "lemma",
          "title": "Weighted analytic polygon functions have corner decay and scaled analytic bounds",
          "deps": [
            "def-countable-choice",
            "def-sobolev-space-wkp-and-its-norm",
            "def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes",
            "thm-fubini-theorem-for-l-one-on-sigma-finite-product-spaces",
            "thm-cauchy-schwarz-in-an-inner-product-space",
            "lem-shape-regular-affine-simplex-scaling",
            "lem-smooth-bump-between-concentric-euclidean-balls",
            "def-mollifier-family-generated-by-a-unit-mass-smooth-bump",
            "def-l-one-approximate-identity-on-rn",
            "prop-mollifier-families-are-l-one-approximate-identities",
            "thm-l-one-approximate-identities-converge-in-l-p",
            "thm-convolution-with-a-mollifier-is-smooth-and-differentiates-under-the-integral-sign",
            "thm-lebesgue-measure-of-a-box-of-every-kind"
          ],
          "justified_by": [],
          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. Let $\\Omega\\subset\\mathbb R^2$ be a bounded open polygonal domain with finitely many straight sides and corner set $\\mathcal C=\\{c_1,\\ldots,c_m\\}$, with interior angle at each corner strictly between $0$ and $2\\pi$. Let $0\\le\\beta_i<1$ and write $\\Phi_\\gamma(x)=\\prod_{i=1}^m|x-c_i|^{\\gamma_i}$ for a vector $\\gamma\\in[0,\\infty)^m$. For integer $k\\ge2$, define\n\n$$\n\\|v\\|_{H^{k,2}_\\beta(\\Omega)}^2=\\|v\\|_{H^1(\\Omega)}^2+\\sum_{j=2}^k\\sum_{|\\alpha|=j}\\|\\Phi_{\\beta+j-2}D^\\alpha v\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}^2,\n$$\n\nwhere $(\\beta+j-2)_i=\\beta_i+j-2$ and a zero exponent contributes the factor one. Let $u\\in H^{k,2}_\\beta(\\Omega)$ for every integer $k\\ge2$, with real-valued weak derivatives, and suppose constants $C_u,d_u>0$ satisfy\n\n$$\n\\left\\|\\Phi_{\\beta+j-2}\\sum_{|\\alpha|=j}|D^\\alpha u|\\right\\|_{L^2(\\Omega)}\\le C_ud_u^{j-2}(j-2)!\\qquad(j\\ge2).\n$$\n\nFor each fixed $0<a<\\min_i(1-\\beta_i)$ there are constants $C,A,R>0$ such that the weak class of $u$ has a unique representative $\\widetilde u\\in C(\\overline\\Omega)$, smooth up to every open side away from corners, and for $0<r=|x-c_i|<R$,\n\n$$\n|\\widetilde u(x)-\\widetilde u(c_i)|\\le Cr^a,\\qquad |D^\\alpha\\widetilde u(x)|\\le CA^{|\\alpha|}|\\alpha|!r^{a-|\\alpha|}\\quad(|\\alpha|\\ge1).\n$$\n\nOn every compact subset of $\\overline\\Omega\\setminus\\mathcal C$, the derivatives satisfy ordinary factorial bounds $|D^\\alpha u|\\le C_0A_0^{|\\alpha|}|\\alpha|!$. On every closed nondegenerate shape-regular affine triangle $K\\subset\\overline\\Omega$ with $K^\\circ\\subset\\Omega$ and $K\\cap\\mathcal C=\\varnothing$, whose ratio $h_K/\\operatorname{dist}(K,\\mathcal C)$ is bounded above and below by fixed positive constants, where $\\operatorname{dist}(K,\\mathcal C)=\\inf_{x\\in K,c\\in\\mathcal C}|x-c|$, set $r_K=\\min(R,\\operatorname{dist}(K,\\mathcal C))$. After subtracting a suitable constant from the pullback $\\widehat u$ to the reference triangle of [[def-matching-affine-simplicial-meshes]], $\\|D^\\alpha\\widehat u\\|_\\infty\\le C A_1^{|\\alpha|}|\\alpha|!r_K^a$ for every multi-index $\\alpha$, with constants uniform over this family. If a closed nondegenerate shape-regular affine triangle $K\\subset\\overline\\Omega$ with $K^\\circ\\subset\\Omega$, diameter $h<R$, has a corner $c_i$ as a vertex, its vertex affine interpolant $a_K$ satisfies\n\n$$\n|u-a_K|_{H^1(K)}\\le Ch^a,\\qquad \\|u-a_K\\|_{L^2(K)}\\le Ch^{a+1}.\n$$",
