          "statement": "Assume Countable Choice. On a fixed finite matching affine tensor-box mesh, let $V=H^1(\\Omega)$ with its standard norm, let $a(v,w)=\\int_\\Omega(\\nabla v\\cdot\\nabla w+vw)$, and let $F$ be a bounded linear functional on $V$. Let $u\\in V$ solve $a(u,w)=F(w)$ for all $w\\in V$, and let $u_p$ be its conforming Galerkin solution in the common-degree trace-matching tensor space of [[def-hp-variable-degree-spaces-on-matching-meshes]]. If the analytic hypotheses of [[thm-hp-analytic-p-convergence-on-fixed-tensor-mesh]] hold with constants $M,R$ and $R^{-1}<q<1$, then\n$$\n\\|u-u_p\\|_{H^1(\\Omega)}\\le C_{\\mathcal T,d,R,q}M q^p.\n$$\nThis is the fixed-mesh analytic branch; it does not assert an h-dependent estimate or an ordinary Sobolev p-rate on simplices.",
