equality of those traces. Common image topology is given by the homeomorphism $G\\circ F^{-1}$.\n\nFor each finite cell, the rational expression has a smooth extension to a neighborhood of its closed rectangle: its polynomial numerator and denominator extend there and the denominator remains positive after shrinking the neighborhood. Its second derivatives are therefore bounded on that closed cell. For a sequence of grids, uniform reference-simplex shape regularity follows if $\\max_r\\ell_r/\\min_r\\ell_r\\le\\kappa$ on every rectangle with fixed $\\kappa$. Uniform curved-map bounds additionally require uniform first, inverse and second derivative bounds of the rational cell expressions. Neither uniform second derivative bounds nor a shape constant follows from a first derivative error bound alone. The construction changes the geometry presentation only; rational analysis functions remain rational and are not reclassified as affine P1 functions.",
