      "description": "{\"scope\": \"Define characteristic backtracking plus multilinear/barycentric interpolation for linear nonconservative transport on a periodic box or an explicitly resolved inflow/exit branch. Prove maximum/sup-norm stability for nonnegative partition-of-unity interpolation regardless of displacement-to-cell-size ratio. Prove a smooth-solution global error bound distinguishing characteristic foot error, interpolation defect per step and initial/boundary error: for fixed T, a typical bound is C(dt^q+h^(r+1)/dt) when each backtracking step has O(dt^(q+1)) foot error and interpolation has O(h^(r+1)) defect. State the actual joint mesh/time condition; absence of a classical advective CFL does not eliminate consistency constraints. Define a conservative characteristic-cell overlap method and prove mass conservation/positivity separately; pointwise interpolation is not inherently conservative. High-order interpolation receives its actual operator norm/limiter bound, not automatic L∞ contractivity.\", \"proof_route\": \"Characteristic chain rule plus bounded velocity/state derivatives; prove backtracking map stays admissible and handle periodic wrapping/inflow first-hit. Existing ODE local error controls foot error via solution Lipschitz norm. Interpolation convexity proves sup stability; telescope one-step consistency defects with discrete Gronwall. For conservative remapping use Reynolds/Jacobian mass factors for divergence-form transport, orientation/invertibility and partitioned departure-cell measures, then PE17 overlap conservation. Boundary hitting error requires transversal events or exact exit oracle with declared error; no hidden root solve.\", \"examples\": \"rotation across many cells per step, fixed h/dt consistency loss, nonconservative mass drift, conservative deforming-cell remap.\"}",
