  {
    "id": "thm-periodic-semilagrangian-global-error-from-local-defects",
    "kind": "theorem",
    "title": "Periodic semi-Lagrangian error is controlled by local foot and interpolation defects",
    "deps": [
      "alg-semilagrangian-backtracking-on-periodic-grid",
      "def-linear-transport-equation-and-its-characteristic-flow",
      "thm-periodic-c1-velocity-has-global-characteristic-flow",
      "lem-periodic-tensor-interpolant-is-convex-and-linf-contracting",
      "lem-periodic-tensor-interpolation-hessian-error",
      "lem-euler-backward-characteristic-foot-error",
      "thm-chain-rule-for-total-derivatives"
    ],
    "justified_by": [],
    "dependency_level": 3,
    "statement": "Fix $T>0$ and a periodic box with grid width $h=\\max_j h_j$. Let $u\\in C^1([0,T];C^2(\\mathbb T^d_\\ell))$ solve the nonconservative linear transport equation\n$$u_t+b\\cdot\\nabla u=0,$$\nwith the periodic $C^1$ velocity and global flow of [[thm-periodic-c1-velocity-has-global-characteristic-flow]]. Consider $N$ equal time steps $\\Delta t=T/N$ and node updates\n$U_{\\boldsymbol i}^{n+1}=(\\mathcal J_h U^n)(\\widetilde x_{\\boldsymbol i}^{\\,n}),$\nwhere $\\mathcal J_h$ reconstructs a nodal array as a periodic function and $\\widetilde x_{\\boldsymbol i}^{\\,n}$ is a computed backward foot. Suppose constants $\\Lambda\\ge1$, $C_I\\ge0$, and $C_F\\ge0$ are uniform over the refinement family and independent of $h,\\Delta t,N$. Assume $\\|\\mathcal J_hV-\\mathcal J_hW\\|_{L^\\infty}\\le\\Lambda\\|V-W\\|_{\\ell^\\infty}$ for all node arrays, the pointwise interpolation defect at each computed foot is at most $C_Ih^{r+1}$ for the exact samples $u^n_{\\boldsymbol i}=u(x_{\\boldsymbol i},t_n)$, and, for compatible lifts of the computed and exact feet, the foot error satisfies\n$\\|\\widetilde x_{\\boldsymbol i}^{\\,n}-X(t_n;t_{n+1},x_{\\boldsymbol i})\\|_2\\le C_F(\\Delta t)^{q+1}$,\nfor integers $q,r\\ge1$. If $L_u:=\\sup_{[0,T]\\times\\mathbb T^d_\\ell}\\|\\nabla u\\|_2$ and $E_n:=\\max_{\\boldsymbol i}|U_{\\boldsymbol i}^n-u(x_{\\boldsymbol i},t_n)|$, then, with\n$$\\delta_h:=C_Ih^{r+1}+\\Lambda L_u C_F(\\Delta t)^{q+1},$$\n$$E_N\\le\\Lambda^NE_0+\\delta_h\\sum_{k=0}^{N-1}\\Lambda^k.$$\nIn the contractive case $\\Lambda=1$, this becomes\n$$E_N\\le E_0+T\\left(C_I\\frac{h^{r+1}}{\\Delta t}+L_uC_F(\\Delta t)^q\\right).$$\nFor the explicit Euler and tensor multilinear algorithm, [[lem-euler-backward-characteristic-foot-error]], [[lem-periodic-tensor-interpolation-hessian-error]], and [[lem-periodic-tensor-interpolant-is-convex-and-linf-contracting]] give $q=r=1$ and $\\Lambda=1$. Thus convergence for this branch follows, for example, when $E_0\\to0$, $\\Delta t\\to0$, and $h^2/\\Delta t\\to0$. No classical advective CFL restriction is used; the joint consistency refinement is still required by this bound.",
